# Each phrase inflates a count without giving it, so the fix names the
# items or writes `many` or `several` (`a wide range of styles` becomes
# `the serif, sans, and mono styles`). The fix does not give the count,
# because a count of a set that can grow goes stale.
#
# `a host of` skips a following determiner (a word that introduces a
# noun, such as `the`, `a`, or `this`), where `host` names a machine (`a
# host of the cluster`).
#
# `a significant number of` and its kin with `huge`, `substantial`,
# `considerable`, or `good` report here. `a large number of` stays out,
# because the Required ProseWordy rule reports it. `a certain number of`
# and `a limited number of` stay out, because `many` changes or reverses
# their meaning. `a large amount of` stays out, because `many` does not
# fit a noun with no plural (`memory`).
#
# The Optional rule of the same name holds `various`.
#
# It hit 46 lines in the measure.py corpus, and 18 of 20 sampled hits
# stood for a count that the sentence did not give. The misses used
# `variety` for a kind (`lifetimes: a variety of generics`) or for
# `different` (`values with a variety of types`).
expr main [(rich set), (wide range), (wide variety), (plethora of), (myriad of), (a myriad), (wide array), (vast array), (broad range), (diverse range), (a host of ![the, this, that, a, an, each, every, its, their]), (a whole host), (a slew of), countless, numerous, (a variety of), (a [huge, significant, substantial, considerable, good] number of)]
let message "Vague quantity. Name the items, or write `many` or `several`."
let description "Flags phrases such as `wide range` and `plethora of` that inflate a count without giving it."
let becomes ""
let kind "Style"
allows "The catalog holds forty styles."
allows "The range covers ports 1 through 1024."
allows "Drain a host of the cluster before the upgrade."
allows "The job retries five times."
